-- title:
--   True original randomly stopped discounted generator drift loses no negative-mark L¹ mass in finite-band passage
-- statement:
--   With the literal original spectrally negative Lévy X.X, X.ν, controlled prepayment reserve x+X.X−rightLimit D and inclusive original ruinTime, for any original rightCont stopping time τ, q≥0 and finite T, the original source nonlinear C² generator jump drift weighted by 1_{s≤T}exp(-qs)1_{s≤τ} has physical L¹ tail tending to zero on every shrinking measurable negative Lévy-mark set. This applies the previously verified arbitrary bounded predictable physical generator L1 tail theorem a5242e78 and accepted original stopping-weight theorem 7b979a09; no source jump isometry, no finite first moment of large negative marks, and no generic compensator substitution.
-- source:
